{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789774293,"nonce":"YZff7qrIcjqy92FDonGmKfdYglA=","message":"Plan agreed 2026-09-18 after the Typed AST review: the frontend stops inventing a tuple representation and uses the compiler's `Type::Tuple`, in steps that each leave the suite green.\n\n1. `Ty::Tuple(u16)` names a shape in an interned table (element Tys, nested); `ir()` maps it to `Type::Tuple`, literals to `TypedExpression::Tuple`, unpacking to per-field `Index`, constant `t[i]` to `Index` (ExtractValue), `len` to a constant, concatenation to a wider shape. Joins are element-wise at equal arity, `Object` otherwise. A tuple boxes only at a dynamic edge (`Object`, a `List\u003cAny\u003e` element, a global, a field): `Tuple -\u003e Object` builds today's tagged `List\u003cAny\u003e`; `Object -\u003e Tuple` checks tag and length and unboxes each field. Lists of tuples stay `Elem::Object` in this step.\n2. `Elem::Tuple(u16)`: `List\u003cTuple\u003e` with struct elements. The list library's per-kind generator (`lists::kind_declarations`) is instantiated per shape with element-wise eq/lt/repr and per-field box/unbox; that is the monomorphization. Boxed lists of tuples carry a per-shape tag with frontend hooks for element reads, as instances do.\n3. Shaped dicts (24cef98) so `BODIES.values()` is a `List\u003cTuple\u003e`; this is what reaches nbody_modified's inner loop.\n4. Per-shape function instances where one function is called with different shapes; until then such a parameter joins to `Object`.\n\nPrerequisites landed: e23434a (nested aggregate fields in Cranelift), 17b81e6 (single-scalar struct Load/Store).","files":null}]}